 @JoshuaBardwell  That's exactly it, and why my content isn't in this area - I just can't put explanations at the right level, it's just middle school or grad school, whereas you, Mark, and Chris do a fantastic job of that.
Being able to make troubleshooting seem logical and well-ordered, that's why you're full time.  Plain and simple, you make this sport accessible to not complete nerds.  It's arguably insane that Chris can actually make finite element analysis VV&A something that can actually be a popular discussion topic, which is crazy.  The discussions I've had as an output of that, including some with Chris, have been intensely enlightening as well.
I guess I'm grumpy about how much I'll be trying to put out fires in a few groups and discords with people who are following about 80% of this method and having all sorts of problems with it.  No intention of gatekeeping on this, but there will be some growing pains with getting all of that work, and SliderGate was kinda an extension of that.

